s permanently scrambled. Most of all, prepare to be wrong. Wrong about what you thought you'd see. Wrong about what "starving" looks like. Wrong about the capacity of human beings to endure, to smile, to create beauty, all while carrying a hidden burden in every cell of their being. You weren't dumb. You were the one insisting on the full, painful truth. I was the one trying to sell you a softer version because I was afraid you'd cancel your trip or fall into pity. You refused. And you were right. Thank you for that.
